# 019 · A rig-only entry, with TLS

**Status:** `READY` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Rigs on RunPod

## What

Control offers a second entry that serves only the rig paths (`/v1/rigs/*`) over HTTPS, so rigs on other networks can report while the dashboard stays private. TLS is native or behind a documented proxy. The signing key comes from a file or a secret.

## Why

A RunPod rig, or any rig on another network, must reach control over the internet. Rigs dial out, so a rig host needs no open port.

## Done when

- [ ] A rig on another network enrolls and reports through the entry.
- [ ] The dashboard and the API cannot be reached through it.
- [ ] The docs show both TLS options.

## Decisions

None yet.

## Open questions

- How rigs reach control: a public rig-only entry (recommended), or a mesh VPN inside the pod.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.

